---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/utils';
import CoffeeCorner from '../components/CoffeeCorner.astro';
import LondonGuide from '../components/LondonGuide.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="About Robin Saini | Engineering, Agentic AI, Coffee & London Life"
  description="The story of Robin Saini: Lead / Senior Data Engineer in London, specialty coffee brewing enthusiast, AI data engineer, and city explorer."
>
  <div class="about-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-badge-row">
        <span class="badge badge-coffee">Biography &amp; Passions</span>
        <span class="badge">Beyond the Resume</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="heading-xl about-title">
        The Journey: <span class="text-gradient-ai">Pipelines</span>, <span class="text-gradient-ai">AI Data Engineering</span>, and <span class="text-gradient-coffee">Specialty Brews</span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="about-intro">
        I'm a London-based Lead / Senior Data Engineer with 15+ years in technology. When I'm not orchestrating 50+ source Snowflake platforms or building trustworthy data for AI agents, you'll find me pulling morning flat whites on my <strong>Sage Barista Pro</strong> &amp; <strong>DF54 flat burrs</strong>, dialing in unimodal pour-overs on my <strong>1Zpresso ZP6 Special</strong> with strictly London-roasted beans, brewing draft beer at home with my <strong>Pinter</strong>, stamping my <strong>London Beer Passport</strong> across microbreweries and historic pubs, hunting down the city's finest artisan sourdough loaves, or, on weekends, watching Formula 1, cheering on Lewis Hamilton at Ferrari and enjoying all the engineering and technicalities behind it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container about-body">
    <!-- Story Timeline Section -->
    <section class="story-section">
      <h2 class="heading-lg story-heading">My Engineering Evolution</h2>

      <div class="timeline-grid">
        <div class="card timeline-card">
          <div class="timeline-period font-mono">2011 – 2016</div>
          <h3 class="heading-sm timeline-title">The Foundation: Mainframes &amp; DB2</h3>
          <p class="timeline-desc">
            Started with COBOL and IBM DB2 systems under rigorous ITIL incident and change management. This taught me system resilience, deterministic transaction integrity, and respect for business-critical core ledgers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card timeline-card">
          <div class="timeline-period font-mono">2016 – 2021</div>
          <h3 class="heading-sm timeline-title">The Shift: Enterprise Data Platform Modernisation</h3>
          <p class="timeline-desc">
            At Lloyds Banking Group (via TCS), led data services teams, built scalable ETL pipelines that reduced load times by 50%, and worked on Teradata modernisation as part of the enterprise data platform, exploring a move to Google BigQuery.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card timeline-card">
          <div class="timeline-period font-mono">2021 – 2025</div>
          <h3 class="heading-sm timeline-title">Modern Lakehouse Scale: NatWest ESG Platform</h3>
          <p class="timeline-desc">
            Built customer, mortgage and deposit data marts for retail leadership, then led the team delivering NatWest's ESG and climate data platform on Snowflake with Airflow and dbt: 50+ sources, 1TB+/month, a Data Guardian framework for contracts and data quality, third-party enrichment, and emissions data products on a data marketplace. Batch times fell 40% and data quality incidents 30%.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card timeline-card highlight-timeline">
          <div class="timeline-period font-mono">2025 – Present</div>
          <h3 class="heading-sm timeline-title">The Frontier: AI Data Engineering at NatWest</h3>
          <p class="timeline-desc">
            Leading data engineering for agentic AI projects at NatWest: connecting agents to data sources, giving them trustworthy datasets and context, and building reusable MCP servers, Pydantic validation gates and observability. The agentic workflows cut manual investigation time by over 90%. <a href={url('/#agentic')}>See the Agentic Lab →</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- My Core Philosophy -->
    <section class="philosophy-section">
      <div class="card philosophy-card">
        <h2 class="heading-md">How I Think About Engineering</h2>
        <div class="philosophy-grid">
          <div>
            <h4 class="phil-title">1. Determinism Over Vibes</h4>
            <p class="phil-text">
              Whether building an agentic loop or a PySpark aggregation, don't let models or scripts guess. Use typed data contracts, deterministic Python math, and Pydantic schemas.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="phil-title">2. Decouple Tooling with MCP</h4>
            <p class="phil-text">
              Agents should never write ad-hoc database queries. Expose standardized, sandboxed Model Context Protocol servers so multiple agents share clean, audited interfaces.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="phil-title">3. Measure and Observability First</h4>
            <p class="phil-text">
              Track tool-call latency, schema validation failures, and model reasoning drift in Splunk and automated LLM-as-a-judge pipelines.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- Personal sections -->
  <CoffeeCorner />
  <LondonGuide />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    padding: 5rem 0 3.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.04) 0%, transparent 100%);
  }

  .section-badge-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-title {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 960px;
  }

  .about-intro {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .about-body {
    padding: 4rem 0 2rem 0;
  }

  .story-section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .story-heading {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .timeline-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .timeline-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .timeline-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .highlight-timeline {
    border-color: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.4);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08) 0%, var(--bg-card) 100%);
  }

  .timeline-period {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent-coffee-light);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .timeline-title {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .timeline-desc {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.925rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .philosophy-section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .philosophy-card {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border-color: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.3);
  }

  .philosophy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .philosophy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .phil-title {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .phil-text {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
